{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_slice_6a", "label": "Slice 6a \u2014 A Real Corpus Survives, and Files Go In From a Browser", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Closes the pipeline's input end: a nested corpus could not be scanned at all, and ingest read whole files into memory."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_recursive_walk", "label": "Recursive Ingest Walk (depth 16)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Depth 16 is not a loop guard \u2014 symlinked directories are not followed, which is free because DirEntry::file_type() does not traverse \u2014 but a bound on pathological nesting and bind mounts that can cycle. Dot-entries are skipped; unreadable subdirectories are logged and skipped, because one unreadable folder must not cost the other 3,999 files. The whole relative path sorts, not the basename."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_source_path_identity", "label": "Identity Moves From the Name to the Path", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Recursion alone is silent data loss: brackets/bracket.stl and plates/bracket.stl both become the part 'bracket', the second violates the name constraint, and classify_write maps that to Skipped \u2014 so the file is reported as already here and never indexed. Two parts called bracket in different folders is the truth, and the path is what tells them apart. All three sites move in one commit."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_migration_0007", "label": "Migration 0007 \u2014 source_path", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Backfilled from existing rows, which are all flat by construction because the scan that created them could not descend; a part with no source file row falls back to name alone, so the backfill cannot strand a row."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_streaming_io", "label": "Streaming Instead of Buffering", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The mesh kernel needs the whole mesh in memory to tessellate, so ingest goes from two copies to one rather than to none; download can go to constant memory because it only forwards bytes. Measured: streaming peaks at 5.7 MB against 385.8 MB buffering the same 380 MB blob. Reverting it is behaviourally identical and no test can catch it, which is why the criterion is a measurement."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_streamed_verification_promise", "label": "The Verification Promise Changes Shape", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Verifying before the first byte is buffering, so streaming cannot keep it. Bytes are hashed incrementally and a mismatch closes the body early, with Content-Length from blob.size_bytes so a short read is detectable. The promise moves from 'we never begin sending unverified bytes' to 'we never finish a download whose bytes did not verify'."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_source_writer", "label": "SourceWriter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The mirror of SourceReader, and the reasoning comes out the other way round: gating this behind WorkerRole would hand the api get and remove on every source blob in order to buy a put. Verification lives in the store, not the route, because 'store these bytes and they must hash to X' is the content-addressed store's own invariant and a route that verified separately would read a 2 GB file twice."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_upload_routes", "label": "Probe / Chunk / Commit Upload Routes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The probe answers three lists rather than DATA.md's two, because the second win is the larger one: re-importing a folder into a new library transfers nothing. Commit is one batch for the whole folder \u2014 committing per file would give a folder of 500 parts 500 progress bars."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_staging_file_is_session", "label": "The Staging File's Length Is the Session State", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "No session table, no session id, no expiry sweep and no in-memory map. Resuming is offset = length; a wrong offset is a 409 carrying the length the server actually has, so a client that lost track is told rather than guessed at. The hash is the session id and is parsed as 64 lowercase hex before it reaches the filesystem, so there is no client string in that path at all."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_zero_refcount_blob_row", "label": "The api Inserts the blob Row at ref_count 0", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Splitting the write and the mesh across two processes creates a new orphan class the reap-on-failure trick cannot reach, because the failing process did not write the bytes and must not assume it may delete them. A blob row with count zero is collectable by slice 7's reaper; an orphan with no row at all is invisible to it forever. It also makes the worker's arm shorter, because link_existing then runs unchanged."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_path_escapes", "label": "path_escapes Predicate in lapidary-core", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "One predicate, two doors: the scan payload joins against ingest_dir, and a client-supplied source_path goes into part.source_path and from there into a Content-Disposition filename. A guard on the caller rather than on the door is the shape that leaves a sibling caller unprotected."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_webkit_relative_path", "label": "webkitRelativePath Keeps the Dropped Folder's First Segment", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Stripping it makes two dropped folders collide on a shared basename, which the source_path constraint turns into one part indexed and one silently skipped. readEntries also returns at most 100 entries per call, so calling it once reads the first hundred files of a parts library and drops the rest."}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_slice_6a", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_slice_5", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_recursive_walk", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_source_path_identity", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_source_path_identity", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_migration_0007", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_migration_0007", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_part_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_migration_0007", "target": "specs_2026_09_03_phase_1_slice_2_jobs_design_part_name_unique_per_library", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_source_path_identity", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_library_holds", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_recursive_walk", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_lapidary_ingest", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_recursive_walk", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_path_escapes", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_path_escapes", "target": "specs_2026_09_01_phase_0a_foundation_design_lapidary_core", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_streaming_io", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_source_store", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_streaming_io", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_download_route", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_streamed_verification_promise", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_rehash_before_serving", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_streamed_verification_promise", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_streaming_io", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_source_writer", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_source_reader", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_source_writer", "target": "specs_2026_09_05_phase_1_slice_5_browser_design_check_open_path_boundary", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_upload_routes", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_source_writer", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-phase-1-slice-6a-corpus-design.md", "source_location":